The code-level pushforward of an element x of the first neighbourhood system is the element of the second system whose members are the basic neighbourhoods of X-sequence codes n such that x contains the basic neighbourhood of index n. Subset closure is the unconditional genuineness of those codes, the master is the code at index 0 once the zeroth basic neighbourhood is the master, a binary intersection is named by surjectivity and transported by the intersection equation for X-sequence codes, and upward closure is the separate upward-membership lemma.
